  "id": "explicit-emotion-regulation",
  "term": "explicit emotion regulation",
  "definition": "Explicit emotion regulation is the conscious, deliberate effort to increase or decrease emotions in line with a known goal. It involves awareness that one is trying to regulate emotion and may use intentional, top-down strategies such as changing how one thinks about a situation.",
